WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.420
If you want to hear the theory about how everything
in this movie ties back to the original train

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.800
crash in Unbreakable, then stick around to
the end of this video.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.710
Welcome back to Things You Missed and Happy
Halloween -- this will probably be the last

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.710
episode I get to put up this October.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.710
It went by so fast.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.609
One thing that did not go by fast was the
wait between Unbreakable and Split.

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:27.710
That was a 16 year wait.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.220
So with that in mind, waiting until January
for the third movie in the franchise, Glass,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.190
to come out, doesn’t seem as bad.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.830
Until then, we’ve got a second trailer,
and I’ve got some things you missed.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:40.370
You may have noticed the strong color scheme
on display in Glass.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.800
Elijah Price has a lot of purples, in his
clothes, in his shoes, in his stuff; he’s

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.780
the villain and the villains section in the
comic book store is purple, and this is also

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.860
kind of like his movie in the series and all
the the titles are purple to signify that.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.560
Then there’s The Horde and his color is
yellow, like if you look at his comic book

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.910
pages, the indicator lights on these machines
in his room and almost all of his outfits.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:05.379
Some of the rooms are either painted or lit
to match these colors and there is line suggesting

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:07.609
that Elijah and the Horde could team up,

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.570
“That sounds like the bad guys teaming up.”

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.600
...which may be the reason this room is striped
in yellow and purple.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.240
David Dunn is green, the color of his iconic
rain poncho from the first movie until now,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.390
and the color of his outfit at the mental
institution matches that, and the heroes section

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.139
of the comic book store is green as well.

00:01:25.139 --> 00:01:29.149
The respective characters’ colors are made
very obvious in the poster, though I do hope

00:01:29.149 --> 00:01:33.110
we get another poster at some point with the
cracked glass on it to match up with the Split

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.570
and Unbreakable posters that fit together
when laid out, side by side.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.289
You can also see each of their colors represented
in different rooms on the security monitors

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:41.649
if you pause right here.

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:44.280
You may be wondering why there is so much
focus on these colors.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.440
I recommend you go pay attention to the movies.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.240
Peace.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.100
No, OK fine.

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:57.080
I think the colors are there to represent
David’s innate ability to sense evil.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:01.119
He has this sense, A Sixth Sense if you will.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:03.520
OK I really have to stop trying to put jokes
in my videos.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.630
In the first movie, we see that if David touches
someone, he can see the bad things that they’ve

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.300
done and he can track bad people in a crowd
because their color will stand out to him

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.050
and become much more saturated.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.270
So I think purple and yellow are their villain
colors, as seen by David.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.060
Once David and The Horde are captured and
put into the institution, the woman studying

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.310
them, her name’s Dr. Staple, has individual
methods for keeping them all in check.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.480
For Elijah, they keep him sedated, because
apparently he’s become such a good manipulator,

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.610
they can’t even handle him if he’s fully
awake.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.740
"He's too smart for them."

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:37.890
David’s room is filled with these pipes
and nozzles because his weakness is water,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.390
so they can give him a spray whenever he becomes
unruly.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:46.860
This would also be an effective room for scientists
to study the aliens from Signs, don’t you

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.970
think?

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.860
The method that they used to keep The Horde
under control is pretty much explained verbatim

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.860
in the trailer.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.340
“The light will force a different identity
to take over.”

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.390
“Por favor, senor.”

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.140
“I want my headphones back.”

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.940
“Step away from the controls now little
darling.”

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.340
“Can’t beat The Beast!”

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.870
When I did the video talking about the first
Glass trailer, I

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.730
wondered why Dr. Staple didn’t have The
Horde chained down like David Dunn.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.250
In this trailer, you can see that the flashing
lights are set up behind her so she can change

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.980
him to a different personality if things get
dicey.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.200
The fact that these are the weaknesses is
very interesting to me, and here’s why.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.680
Think back to Unbreakable.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.220
One of the most iconic scenes in that movie,
heck, one of the most iconic scenes in cinema,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.010
is the scene where he rescues the kidnapped
kids in the rain, almost drowning in the pool

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.640
as he does so.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.260
That’s an epic scene, but imagine what the
final showdown could be like in Glass.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.460
The fight breaks through a glass window into
a thunderstorm.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.930
David is dramatically weakened by the water,
but the intermittent flashes of lightning

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:02.090
cause the Horde to be constantly changing
personalities, throwing him into complete

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.350
disarray.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.740
So it will come down to Elijah to think of
some clever solution.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.070
When I did the Things You Missed on the first
Glass trailer, I broke down this entire comic

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.650
that appears on screen and I talked about
how this character could represent either

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.900
The Horde or David, because of his desire
to protect people.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.800
In this trailer we get a glimpse at another
panel of this comic.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.350
It says: “I vowed to protect everyone from
those of us given these cruel gifts.”

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.270
That line suggests that this is more likely
representative of David.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:36.870
"Why is it do you think that of all the professions
in the world, you chose protection?"

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.910
However, I wouldn’t also rule out the possibility
that this is a sign that The Beast will change

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.330
sides, and realize that he wants to be a good
guy.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.490
Also, I think they’ve already learned their
lesson about The Beast’s ability to bend

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.220
bars, because it looks like in his room, he’s
got bricks for windows.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.750
Next there’s a scene in which Elijah sneaks
into the record room and accesses The Horde’s

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:55.750
medical file.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.810
Let’s pause on that and take a closer look.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:02.340
You’ll notice some of the names of the identities
familiar to us from Split, such as Rakel,

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.820
Luke, Polly, Bernice and of course, The Beast.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:09.350
We know this because each identity has a file
on the computer in Split.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:13.930
However, there are some new names here, like
this name ending in “--elida” and this

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.930
name ending in the letters “MA”.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:19.510
So this could be evidence that there are still
new personalities emerging within The Horde,

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:23.540
just as The Beast emerged as a 24th personality
back in Split.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.380
Speaking of The Beast, the first time Kevin’s
body transformed into The Beast was at a train

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.590
station in Split.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.130
The backstory is glossed over and we find
out in that movie that Kevin’s dad left

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.080
on a train when he was a child and never came
back -- leading some to believe that this

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.700
emotional damage caused the identity disorder,
and some to theorize that the train he left

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:45.960
on was Eastrail 177, the train that crashed
and left David Dunn as the only survivor.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.630
I bring this all up because the new trailer
reveals a scene taking place in what appears

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:54.560
to be a hobo camp inside of a subway station
and The Beast is the one who exploring it.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.510
And probably scaring the hobos so bad.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:06:00.790
I mean, could you imagine hiding in an abandoned
tunnel and all the sudden this approaches

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.790
you?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:06.650
There is one other possible callback hidden
in this trailer, and that is when Elijah Price

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.730
is addressing David at the microphone.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.730
“David.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:13.330
I found someone who will require your full
potential."

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:17.930
This monologue is very reminiscent of the
voicemails Elijah leaves on David’s answering

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:22.120
machine in Unbreakable, where he tries to
encourage him to embrace his super-hero side.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:23.620
"David?

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.120
It's Elijah.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.060
It was so obvious.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.100
It was this one issue that brought it back
for me.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:34.100
This group, the coalition of evil tried to
ascertain the weakness of every superhero,

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.280
because they all have one."

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.740
Alright, I do a have a few more Things You
Missed, but not a whole lot to say about them.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:44.110
The first is in this shot, and while we’re
focused on Elijah, some dude gets wrecked

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:47.840
by The Beast in the background -- that’s
a super interesting choice to have the action

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.930
play out as a barely noticeable background
detail, so I’m interested to see how that

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.000
plays out in the actual movie.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.720
Then in this shot, I noticed David Dunn’s
son Joseph holding his arm as if he’s injured.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.410
Joseph always believed that his Dad was a
superhero, and there are a few instances where

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.340
he puts his dad in dangerous situations to
try to prove it.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.200
I have to wonder if he starts to believe he
has inherited these same powers, and that’s

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.389
how he gets himself hurt, or if one of the
bad guys targets him to try to rattle David.

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:16.781
Towards the end of the trailer, Elijah can
be spotted wearing this necklace with the

00:07:16.781 --> 00:07:18.090
initials MG.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:21.820
I'm assuming that stands for Mr. Glass, and
if that's true then it seems like Elijah's

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:25.120
really playing in to his super villain persona.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.890
Then we've got a shot of Casey Cooke from
Split getting off of this bus, and this is

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:32.770
actually the same bus that David gets off
in his neighborhood in Unbreakable.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:36.690
Now, it's hard to say if that's an actual
reference to Unbreakable or if this is just

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:40.699
a common bus-line in Philadelphia, so if any
of you guys are from Philly, feel free to

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:42.380
let me know in the comments.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.509
So I’ve got several videos in the pipeline
right now.

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:47.310
As I mentioned this is probably the last of
the October uploads.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:51.530
I know I had also expressed interest in doing
an episode on the Happy Death Day 2U trailer.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.260
That’s because I thought it was out already
-- but they haven’t actually put it online

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.759
yet, despite the fact that it is playing in
front of Halloween in theaters right now.

00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:02.669
I would like to wait for that to come out
on YouTube before I do the Things You Missed

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:03.669
episode.

00:08:03.669 --> 00:08:07.139
And I know there has been a lot Things You
Missed lately, and there is a reason for that.

00:08:07.139 --> 00:08:10.919
A lot of you have been asking where the next
Al Dente Creepypasta is, for those of you

00:08:10.919 --> 00:08:14.210
who don’t know, that’s my scary story
narration series, I’ve got some new episodes

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:17.550
planned, so that should be back soon as well.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:21.560
And I have decided to do a little marathon
leading up to the release of Glass, I’ll

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:26.780
be doing Things You Missed on Unbreakable
and Split, so if you are a fan of this thriller-horror

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:30.770
series, which I’m imagining you are if you’ve
made it this far in the video, then remember

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:36.700
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every
week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.890
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.700
Assuming we both survive.

